# Machine-local vendoring policy: internal product vocabulary that must never reach a published
# artifact. The root .npmignore names it too, but package.json's `files` allowlist takes precedence
# over root ignore rules for everything inside a listed directory — measured here: with the allowlist
# in place and no file like this one, `npm pack` put policy.local.json back into the tarball. A nested
# ignore is still consulted inside an allowlisted directory, so this file is what actually keeps it out,
# and scripts/check-pack-coverage.cjs fails if it ever appears in the artifact.
policy.local.json
